Subject: AOT generator skeleton: binding, entry/exit and the runtime ABI

What this does
  Adds phase P2 of .local/aot-regvm-impl-plan.md: the runtime side that lets a
  generated C unit run register-compiled functions. A function that matches a
  unit entry by its 128-bit content digest is bound at bytecode finalisation
  (aot_fn/aot_state on JSFunctionBytecode) and, when it is called, js_regvm_execute
  hands the already-set-up frame to the generated body instead of entering the
  interpreter loop.

  quickjs-aot-rt.h is the ABI the generated code is compiled against:
  JSAotEntry, JSAotFn, QJS_AOT_ABI, the QJS_AOT_COLD_RET / QJS_AOT_SUSPEND
  sentinels, and qjs_aot_step()/qjs_aot_code()/qjs_aot_ret()/qjs_aot_unwind().
  quickjs-aot-gen.h is the host-side generator interface (js_aot_gen_collect,
  js_aot_gen_insn_size) used by tools/aot/qjsaot.c, which is not shipped.

  The generated body is step-only: it calls qjs_aot_step() for each instruction
  and follows the returned ip. qjs_aot_unwind() is the monolith exception walk
  specialised to an entry frame. QJS_AOT_VERIFY additionally recomputes a
  per-function signature at bind time and refuses a unit built from a different
  engine revision; the signature is derived from the same interning-order
  independent digest, so it is stable across processes.

Why we need it
  Phase P1 gave every opcode a one-instruction step form. P2 turns that into a
  linkable unit: enumerate a bundle's functions, emit a C body per function,
  and run those bodies from the real call path. This is the skeleton P3-P7
  build on (coverage, kernels, budget selection, inlining).

What it adds
  quickjs-aot-rt.h
      The generated-code ABI (types, ABI constant, sentinels, entry points).
  quickjs-aot-gen.h
      The host generator interface used by tools/aot/qjsaot.c.
  quickjs.c
      JSFunctionBytecode.aot_fn/aot_state; eager digest binding at the three
      bytecode-finalisation sites; the AOT entry in js_regvm_execute; the
      runtime block (weak unit table, aot_unit_present, js_aot_bind,
      qjs_aot_step/code/ret/unwind, QJS_AOT_STATS counters); the generator
      collection block (QJS_AOT_GEN); the shared QJS_AOT/QJS_AOT_GEN/QJS_AOT_VERIFY
      knobs. QJS_AOT requires the monolith register build.

  Nothing here is compiled without -DQJS_REGVM; QJS_AOT is off by default and
  the plain register build is byte-for-byte unchanged. Box2D runs fully
  compiled with checksum 546.1008391043414 and test262-fast stays at 50/81192.

